      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What does Hana’s wafer processing cover?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Wafer processing covers backgrind, singulation by laser grooving with blade dicing or full laser cut, and wafer-level inspection before die attach and package assembly.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Which wafer materials can you dice?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Laser grooving with blade dicing is qualified for low-K and GaN. SiC, sapphire and glass use full laser cutting, with an 8 µm laser spot and eight-beam split, and saw streets down to 10 µm.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can you handle thin and fragile wafers?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Thinning includes post-grind stress relief and carrier-based handling, with dicing recipes adjusted to reduce chipping on brittle or thinned die.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Do you keep traceability from wafer to package?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Wafer-map and lot data are carried through singulation into assembly, maintaining material and lot traceability.</div>
    </details>
